# Input OTP

An accessible field for one-time passwords and verification codes. Compose it from `InputOTP`, `InputOTPGroup`, `InputOTPSlot`, and `InputOTPSeparator`. It has no dependencies beyond the theme.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { InputOTP, InputOTPGroup, InputOTPSlot, InputOTPSeparator } from "#lib/components/ui/input-otp/index.js";
</script>

<InputOTP maxlength={6}>
	<InputOTPGroup>
		<InputOTPSlot index={0} />
		<InputOTPSlot index={1} />
		<InputOTPSlot index={2} />
	</InputOTPGroup>
	<InputOTPSeparator />
	<InputOTPGroup>
		<InputOTPSlot index={3} />
		<InputOTPSlot index={4} />
		<InputOTPSlot index={5} />
	</InputOTPGroup>
</InputOTP>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/input-otp.json
```

## Anatomy

`InputOTP` holds the value and the style settings, and shares them with its parts. It renders one transparent native `input` stretched over the slots, so typing, pasting, deleting, and one-time code autofill all work like a normal text field. Each `InputOTPSlot` shows the character at its `index`. `InputOTPGroup` joins its slots with shared borders and rounds the outer corners. `InputOTPSeparator` renders `role="separator"` between groups.

Set `maxlength` to the number of slots. While the field has focus, the slot that receives the next character shows a focus ring and a blinking caret. The caret stays after the last character, so Backspace always removes the last one.

## Pattern

Set `pattern` to a regular expression source that the whole value must match. Typed or pasted text that breaks it is ignored. The default is `REGEXP_ONLY_DIGITS`, which also opens the number pad on touch keyboards. Use `REGEXP_ONLY_CHARS` or `REGEXP_ONLY_DIGITS_AND_CHARS` for letters, or pass your own.

<Demo section="pattern" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { InputOTP, InputOTPGroup, InputOTPSlot, REGEXP_ONLY_DIGITS_AND_CHARS } from "#lib/components/ui/input-otp/index.js";
</script>

<InputOTP maxlength={6} pattern={REGEXP_ONLY_DIGITS_AND_CHARS}>
	<InputOTPGroup>
		{#each { length: 6 }, index (index)}
			<InputOTPSlot {index} />
		{/each}
	</InputOTPGroup>
</InputOTP>
```

Whitespace is removed before the pattern check, so a pasted code such as `123 456` fills all six slots.

## Separator

Pass children to `InputOTPSeparator` to replace the default dash, such as with another icon. Separators scale with the size.

<Demo section="separator" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { InputOTP, InputOTPGroup, InputOTPSlot, InputOTPSeparator } from "#lib/components/ui/input-otp/index.js";
	import { DotIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<InputOTP maxlength={6}>
	<InputOTPGroup>
		<InputOTPSlot index={0} />
		<InputOTPSlot index={1} />
	</InputOTPGroup>
	<InputOTPSeparator><DotIcon /></InputOTPSeparator>
	<InputOTPGroup>
		<InputOTPSlot index={2} />
		<InputOTPSlot index={3} />
	</InputOTPGroup>
	<InputOTPSeparator><DotIcon /></InputOTPSeparator>
	<InputOTPGroup>
		<InputOTPSlot index={4} />
		<InputOTPSlot index={5} />
	</InputOTPGroup>
</InputOTP>
```

## Controlled

Use `bind:value` to read and set the code from your own code, or `onValueChange` to run code when it changes. `onComplete` runs once every slot is filled, such as to submit the code.

Other attributes, such as `id`, `name`, `required`, and `autofocus`, pass through to the native input, so a `Label` with a matching `for` focuses the field and a form submits the value under `name`.

<Demo section="controlled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { InputOTP, InputOTPGroup, InputOTPSlot } from "#lib/components/ui/input-otp/index.js";
	import { Label } from "#lib/components/ui/label/index.js";

	let code = $state("");
</script>

<Label for="otp">Verification code</Label>
<InputOTP id="otp" maxlength={6} bind:value={code} onComplete={(value) => console.log(value)}>
	<InputOTPGroup>
		{#each { length: 6 }, index (index)}
			<InputOTPSlot {index} />
		{/each}
	</InputOTPGroup>
</InputOTP>
<p>Value: {code}</p>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` on `InputOTP` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`, each slot is as tall and wide as the input of the same size, and the corner radius follows the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<InputOTP maxlength={6} size="sm">...</InputOTP>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` on `InputOTP` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius from the size. Only the outer corners of each group are rounded, and `pill` turns each group into a pill.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<InputOTP maxlength={6} rounded="pill">...</InputOTP>
```

## States

Set `disabled` to dim the field and block interaction. Set `aria-invalid="true"` to give every slot the destructive border, such as for a code that failed verification.

<Demo section="states" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<InputOTP maxlength={6} disabled>...</InputOTP>
<InputOTP maxlength={6} aria-invalid="true">...</InputOTP>
```

## Overrides

`InputOTPSlot` takes `size` and `rounded`, which win over the input's for that slot only. The radius shows on the outer corners of each group.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<InputOTPGroup>
	<InputOTPSlot index={0} rounded="pill" />
	<InputOTPSlot index={1} />
</InputOTPGroup>
```

## API

`InputOTP` extends the native `input` attributes and passes them to the hidden input, except `class`, which is merged onto the root container. `InputOTPGroup`, `InputOTPSlot`, and `InputOTPSeparator` extend the native `div` attributes. Slots set `data-active` and `data-invalid` for custom styles.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends Omit<CompProps<"input">, "size" | "value" | "type" | "maxlength" | "pattern" | "class"> {
	/** Characters entered so far; supports `bind:value` */
	value?: string;
	/** Number of characters the code needs; match it to the number of slots */
	maxlength: number;
	/** Regular expression source the whole value must match; defaults to `REGEXP_ONLY_DIGITS` */
	pattern?: string;
	/** Called with the new value when it changes */
	onValueChange?: (value: string) => void;
	/** Called with the value once every slot is filled */
	onComplete?: (value: string) => void;
	/** Slot size, gap, and text size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of each group's outer slots; follows `size` when omitted */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
	/** Groups, slots, and separators */
	children: Snippet;
	/** Classes merged onto the root container */
	class?: CompProps<"div">["class"];
}

interface GroupProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {}

interface SlotProps extends CompProps<"div"> {
	/** Position of the character in the value, starting at 0 */
	index: number;
	/** Size of this slot; overrides the input's `size` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of this slot's outer corners; overrides the input's `rounded` */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

interface SeparatorProps extends CompProps<"div"> {
	/** Custom divider content in place of the dash */
	children?: Snippet;
}
```
